/-!
# The dual formula for the smallest relative entropy to a null generated by constraints

Let `g i`, for `i` in a finite type, be measurable real constraints on a measurable space `𝓧`, and
`Q` a probability measure on `𝓧`. The smallest relative entropy `klInf Q (constraintNull (range g))`
from `Q` to the null `constraintNull (range g)`, written $\mathrm{KL}_{\inf}$ in the bandit
literature, is the largest e-power of the null under `Q`, the largest expected logarithm of an
e-variable for the null, and of a bet `1 + ∑ i, π i * g i`:
$$\inf_{P}\mathrm{KL}(Q,P)=\sup_{\pi}\mathbb E_Q\log\Big(1+\sum_i\pi_ig_i\Big)
=\texttt{maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g))}.$$
The second equality holds for every finite measure `Q`. The first holds as soon as every
`log⁺ |g i|` is `Q`-integrable, with no constraint qualification: no member of the null is asked
to satisfy the constraints strictly, the null may be empty, and both sides may be infinite.

The formulas of Honda and Takemura for one mean constraint on the laws on `[0, 1]` and on
`(-∞, 1]` [HT15] are cases of it, which this file does not derive. The statements and the proof
follow [EVR26, Note 20], whose Lean library EValuesResearch proves them; the proofs here are
adapted from it. The proof does not go through
Lagrange duality, which needs Slater's condition. It compares both sides with the largest expected
logarithm of an e-variable, which Statlib's numeraire [LRR25] attains, and splits along
`exists_measurableSet_noArbitrageOn_or_exists_sum_mul_pos`.

* If a nonnegative combination of the constraints is nonnegative almost surely under the null and
  under `Q`, and positive on a set of positive `Q`-measure, its multiples are bets with unbounded
  expected logarithms, and the three quantities are infinite.
* Otherwise a measurable set `Y` carries the null and `Q`, and the constraints admit no arbitrage
  on `Y`. On `Y` every e-variable is at most a bet, by the complete class theorem
  [LRR26, Theorem 3.1], which gives the second equality. For the
  first, let `E` be the numeraire. The measure with density `1 / E` with respect to `Q`, the
  reverse information projection [LRR25], is damped by `1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|`, so that it integrates the
  constraints, and scaled by `1 - ε`. It is then completed into a member of the null by a finitely
  supported measure on `Y`: the complete class theorem [LRR26, Theorem 3.1], applied to the
  constraints shifted by their means under the damped projection, gives the points and the
  weights. The relative entropy
  from `Q` to that member of the null is at most the largest expected logarithm plus
  `E_Q[log (1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|)] - log (1 - ε)`, which tends to `0` with `δ` and `ε`.

## Main statements

* `ProbabilityTheory.maxEPower_constraintNull_eq_iSup_eintegral_log`: the largest e-power of the
  null equals the supremum of the expected logarithms of the bets.
* `ProbabilityTheory.klInf_constraintNull_eq_maxEPower`: the smallest relative entropy to the null
  is its largest e-power.
* `ProbabilityTheory.klInf_constraintNull_eq_iSup_eintegral_log`: **the dual formula**.

## References

* [EVR26] *Answers to open questions in e-values and anytime-valid inference*, notes 01–34 and the
  Lean library EValuesResearch, github.com/RemyDegenne/evalues_research (2026).
* [HT15] J. Honda and A. Takemura, *Non-asymptotic analysis of a new bandit algorithm for
  semi-bounded rewards*, J. Mach. Learn. Res. 16 (2015).
* [LRR25] M. Larsson, A. Ramdas and J. Ruf, *The numeraire e-variable and reverse information
  projection*, Ann. Statist. 53 (2025), arXiv:2402.18810.
* [LRR26] M. Larsson, A. Ramdas and J. Ruf, *Testing hypotheses generated by constraints*, Math.
  Oper. Res. (2026), arXiv:2504.02974v5.
-/

public section

open MeasureTheory Set InformationTheory LMLExplore
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

namespace ProbabilityTheory

variable {𝓧 ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [MeasurableSpace 𝓧] {g : ι → 𝓧 → ℝ} {Y : Set 𝓧}
  {Q : Measure 𝓧}

/-! ### The damped reverse information projection -/

/-- The density with respect to `Q` of the reverse information projection `Q / E` damped by
`1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|` and scaled by `1 - ε`: `x ↦ (1 - ε) / (E x * (1 + δ ∑ i, |g i x|))`. -/
private noncomputable def dampedDensity (E : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞) (g : ι → 𝓧 → ℝ) (δ ε : ℝ) (x : 𝓧) :
    ℝ≥0∞ :=
  (E x)⁻¹ * ENNReal.ofReal ((1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|))

private lemma measurable_dampedDensity {E : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞} (hE : Measurable E)
    (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) (δ ε : ℝ) : Measurable (dampedDensity E g δ ε) := by
  unfold dampedDensity
  fun_prop

omit [MeasurableSpace 𝓧] in
private lemma dampedDensity_ne_zero {E : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞} {δ ε : ℝ} (hδ : 0 ≤ δ) (hε1 : ε < 1) {x : 𝓧}
    (hx : E x ≠ ∞) : dampedDensity E g δ ε x ≠ 0 := by
  simp only [dampedDensity, ne_eq, mul_eq_zero, ENNReal.inv_eq_zero, hx, ENNReal.ofReal_eq_zero,
    not_le, false_or]
  exact div_pos (by linarith) (by positivity)

/-- The reverse information projection `Q / E` damped by `1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|` and scaled by `1 - ε`
integrates the constraints, as soon as `∫ 1 / E ∂Q` is finite. -/
private lemma integrable_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div {E : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞} (hE : Measurable E)
    (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) (hEinv : ∫⁻ x, (E x)⁻¹ ∂Q ≠ ∞) {δ ε : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ)
    (hε : 0 ≤ ε) (hε1 : ε ≤ 1) (i : ι) :
    Integrable (g i) (Q.withDensity (dampedDensity E g δ ε)) := by
  refine ⟨(hg i).aestronglyMeasurable, ?_⟩
  rw [HasFiniteIntegral, lintegral_withDensity_eq_lintegral_mul _
    (measurable_dampedDensity hE hg δ ε) (by fun_prop)]
  calc ∫⁻ x, (dampedDensity E g δ ε * fun x ↦ ‖g i x‖ₑ) x ∂Q
      ≤ ∫⁻ x, ENNReal.ofReal (1 / δ) * (E x)⁻¹ ∂Q := by
        refine lintegral_mono fun x ↦ ?_
        have hh0 : 0 < 1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x| := by positivity
        have hgi : |g i x| ≤ ∑ j, |g j x| :=
          Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun j ↦ |g j x|) (fun j _ ↦ abs_nonneg _)
            (Finset.mem_univ i)
        have h1 : (1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|) * |g i x| ≤ 1 / δ := by
          rw [div_mul_eq_mul_div, div_le_div_iff₀ hh0 hδ, one_mul]
          have h2 : (1 - ε) * |g i x| * δ ≤ δ * |g i x| := by
            nlinarith [mul_nonneg (mul_nonneg hε hδ.le) (abs_nonneg (g i x))]
          have h3 : δ * |g i x| ≤ δ * ∑ j, |g j x| := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hgi hδ.le
          linarith
        calc (dampedDensity E g δ ε * fun x ↦ ‖g i x‖ₑ) x
            = (E x)⁻¹ * (ENNReal.ofReal ((1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|)) * ‖g i x‖ₑ) := by
              simp only [Pi.mul_apply, dampedDensity, mul_assoc]
          _ = (E x)⁻¹ * ENNReal.ofReal ((1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|) * |g i x|) := by
              rw [Real.eNorm_eq_ofReal_abs, ← ENNReal.ofReal_mul
                (div_nonneg (by linarith) hh0.le)]
          _ ≤ (E x)⁻¹ * ENNReal.ofReal (1 / δ) := by gcongr
          _ = ENNReal.ofReal (1 / δ) * (E x)⁻¹ := mul_comm _ _
    _ = ENNReal.ofReal (1 / δ) * ∫⁻ x, (E x)⁻¹ ∂Q :=
        lintegral_const_mul' _ _ ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top
    _ < ⊤ := ENNReal.mul_lt_top ENNReal.ofReal_lt_top hEinv.lt_top

/-- The mean of a function under the damped and scaled reverse information projection is at most
`1 - ε` times its mean divided by `E` under `Q`. -/
private lemma lintegral_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div_le {E F : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞} (hE : Measurable E)
    (hF : Measurable F) (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) {δ ε : ℝ} (hδ : 0 ≤ δ) (hε1 : ε ≤ 1) :
    ∫⁻ x, F x ∂(Q.withDensity (dampedDensity E g δ ε))
      ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (1 - ε) * ∫⁻ x, F x / E x ∂Q := by
  rw [lintegral_withDensity_eq_lintegral_mul _ (measurable_dampedDensity hE hg δ ε) hF,
    ← lintegral_const_mul' _ _ ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top]
  refine lintegral_mono fun x ↦ ?_
  have : ENNReal.ofReal ((1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|)) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (1 - ε) :=
    ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal (div_le_self (by linarith) (le_add_of_nonneg_right (by positivity)))
  calc (dampedDensity E g δ ε * F) x
      = (E x)⁻¹ * ENNReal.ofReal ((1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|)) * F x := by
        simp only [Pi.mul_apply, dampedDensity]
    _ ≤ (E x)⁻¹ * ENNReal.ofReal (1 - ε) * F x := by gcongr
    _ = ENNReal.ofReal (1 - ε) * (F x / E x) := by rw [div_eq_mul_inv]; ring

/-- The logarithm of the likelihood ratio of `Q` to the damped and scaled reverse information
projection is `log E + log (1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|) - log (1 - ε)`, `Q`-almost everywhere. -/
private lemma log_inv_rnDeriv_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div [SigmaFinite Q] {E : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞}
    (hE : Measurable E) (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) {δ ε : ℝ}
    (hδ : 0 ≤ δ) (hε1 : ε < 1) :
    ∀ᵐ x ∂Q, ENNReal.log (((Q.withDensity (dampedDensity E g δ ε)).rnDeriv Q)⁻¹ x) =
      ENNReal.log (E x) +
        ((Real.log (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|) - Real.log (1 - ε) : ℝ) : EReal) := by
  filter_upwards [Measure.rnDeriv_withDensity Q (measurable_dampedDensity hE hg δ ε)] with x hx
  have hh0 : 0 < 1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x| := by positivity
  have hpos : 0 < (1 - ε) / (1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|) := div_pos (by linarith) hh0
  -- the likelihood ratio is `E x * (1 + δ ∑ j, |g j x|) / (1 - ε)`
  have hinv : (dampedDensity E g δ ε x)⁻¹ =
      E x * ENNReal.ofReal ((1 + δ * ∑ j, |g j x|) / (1 - ε)) := by
    rw [dampedDensity, ENNReal.mul_inv (.inr ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top)
      (.inr (ENNReal.ofReal_pos.2 hpos).ne'), inv_inv, ← ENNReal.ofReal_inv_of_pos hpos, inv_div]
  rw [Pi.inv_apply, hx, hinv, ENNReal.log_mul_add,
    ENNReal.log_ofReal_of_pos (div_pos hh0 (by linarith)), Real.log_div hh0.ne' (by linarith)]

/-- **Completion of the damped reverse information projection**: when `Q` is carried by a set `Y`
without arbitrage that carries the null, and `E` is such that `∫ F / E ∂Q ≤ 1` for every
e-variable `F`, as the numeraire is [LRR25], the reverse information projection `Q / E` damped by
`1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|` and scaled by `1 - ε` becomes a member of the null once a finitely supported
measure is added. -/
private lemma exists_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div_add_sum_smul_dirac_mem_constraintNull
    (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) (hY : NoArbitrageOn g Y)
    (hYμ : ∀ ν ∈ constraintNull (range g), ν Yᶜ = 0) [IsProbabilityMeasure Q] (hQY : Q Yᶜ = 0)
    {E : 𝓧 → ℝ≥0∞} (hE : Measurable E)
    (hEF : ∀ F, IsEVar F (constraintNull (range g)) → ∫⁻ x, F x / E x ∂Q ≤ 1) {δ ε : ℝ}
    (hδ : 0 < δ) (hε : 0 < ε) (hε1 : ε < 1) :
    ∃ (α : Type) (_ : Fintype α) (x : α → 𝓧) (w : α → ℝ),
      Q.withDensity (dampedDensity E g δ ε) +
        ∑ k, ENNReal.ofReal (w k) • Measure.dirac (x k) ∈ constraintNull (range g) := by
  have hYne : Y.Nonempty := by
    by_contra h
    rw [not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at h
    simp [h] at hQY
  have h1 : IsEVar 1 (constraintNull (range g)) :=
    isEVar_one fun _ hν ↦ (isProbabilityMeasure_of_mem_constraintNull hν).measure_univ.le
  have hEinv : ∫⁻ x, (E x)⁻¹ ∂Q ≤ 1 := by simpa using hEF 1 h1
  set μ := Q.withDensity (dampedDensity E g δ ε)
  have hμE : ∀ F, IsEVar F (constraintNull (range g)) →
      ∫⁻ x, F x ∂μ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (1 - ε) := fun F hF ↦
    (lintegral_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div_le hE hF.measurable hg hδ.le hε1.le).trans
      (mul_le_of_le_one_right' (hEF F hF))
  have : IsFiniteMeasure μ :=
    ⟨by simpa using (hμE 1 h1).trans_lt ENNReal.ofReal_lt_top⟩
  obtain ⟨α, _, x, w, -, hP⟩ := exists_add_sum_smul_dirac_mem_constraintNull hg hY hYμ hYne
    (withDensity_absolutelyContinuous Q _ hQY)
    (integrable_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div hE hg (hEinv.trans_lt ENNReal.one_lt_top).ne hδ
      hε.le hε1.le) (ENNReal.ofReal_lt_one.2 (by linarith)) hμE
  exact ⟨α, inferInstance, x, w, hP⟩

/-! ### The nontrivial inequality of the dual formula, on a set without arbitrage -/

/-- The nontrivial inequality of the dual formula, up to a damping `δ` and a slack `ε`: when `Q`
is carried by a set `Y` without arbitrage that carries the null, and the largest expected
logarithm `s` of an e-variable is finite, the reverse information projection `Q / E`, for the
numeraire `E`, damped by `1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|` so that it integrates the constraints, and scaled by
`1 - ε`, is completed into a member of the null by a finitely supported measure, at a relative
entropy at most `s + E_Q[log (1 + δ ∑ i, |g i|)] - log (1 - ε)`. -/
private lemma klInf_constraintNull_le_maxEPower_add (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i))
    (hY : NoArbitrageOn g Y) (hYμ : ∀ ν ∈ constraintNull (range g), ν Yᶜ = 0)
    [IsProbabilityMeasure Q] (hQY : Q Yᶜ = 0)
    (hQ : Integrable (fun x ↦ Real.log (1 + ∑ i, |g i x|)) Q)
    (hs : maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) ≠ ⊤) {δ ε : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ)
    (hδ1 : δ ≤ 1) (hε : 0 < ε) (hε1 : ε < 1) :
    klInf Q (constraintNull (range g)) ≤
      maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) +
        ((∫ x, Real.log (1 + δ * ∑ i, |g i x|) ∂Q - Real.log (1 - ε) : ℝ) : EReal) := by
  have hS : ∀ μ ∈ constraintNull (range g), μ univ ≤ 1 :=
    fun _ hμ ↦ (isProbabilityMeasure_of_mem_constraintNull hμ).measure_univ.le
  set s := maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) with hs_def
  set E := numeraire Q (constraintNull (range g)) with hE_def
  have hEnum := isNumeraire_numeraire Q hS
  have hEm : Measurable E := hEnum.isEVar.measurable
  have hsE : s = ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (E x) ∂Q := maxEPower_eq_eintegral_numeraire hS
  have hE_top : ∀ᵐ x ∂Q, E x ≠ ∞ := by
    have := ae_ne_top_of_eintegral_ne_top (by fun_prop) (hEnum.eintegrable_log hS) (hsE ▸ hs)
    filter_upwards [this] with x hx
    simpa using hx
  -- the damped and scaled reverse information projection, and its completion into a member `P`
  -- of the null
  obtain ⟨α, _, x, w, hP⟩ :=
    exists_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div_add_sum_smul_dirac_mem_constraintNull hg hY hYμ hQY hEm
      (fun F hF ↦ hEnum.lintegral_div_le_one hF) hδ hε hε1
  set μ := Q.withDensity (dampedDensity E g δ ε) with hμ_def
  set P := μ + ∑ k, ENNReal.ofReal (w k) • Measure.dirac (x k) with hP_def
  have := isProbabilityMeasure_of_mem_constraintNull hP
  have hμP : μ ≤ P := Measure.le_add_right le_rfl
  have : IsFiniteMeasure μ := isFiniteMeasure_of_le P hμP
  refine (klInf_le_klIntegral hP).trans ?_
  rw [← maxEPower_singleton measure_univ.le]
  have hμeff : μ ∈ effectiveSet {P} := fun X hX ↦
    calc ∫⁻ x, X x ∂μ ≤ ∫⁻ x, X x ∂P := lintegral_mono' hμP le_rfl
      _ ≤ 1 := hX.lintegral_le_one rfl
  have hac : Q ≪ μ := withDensity_absolutelyContinuous'
    (measurable_dampedDensity hEm hg δ ε).aemeasurable
    (by filter_upwards [hE_top] with x hx using dampedDensity_ne_zero hδ.le hε1 hx)
  have hlogh0 : Integrable (fun x ↦ Real.log (1 + δ * ∑ i, |g i x|)) Q :=
    hQ.log_one_add_const_mul (by fun_prop) (fun x ↦ by positivity) hδ.le hδ1
  have hlogh : Integrable
      (fun x ↦ Real.log (1 + δ * ∑ i, |g i x|) - Real.log (1 - ε)) Q :=
    hlogh0.sub (integrable_const _)
  -- the relative entropy from `Q` to `P` is at most that of the likelihood ratio of `Q` to `μ`
  refine maxEPower_le_iff.2 fun X hX ↦
    (eintegral_log_isEVar_le_eintegral_rnDeriv hμeff hac hX).trans ?_
  have hI := eintegral_eq_integral hlogh
  have hI_bot : ∫ᵉ x, ((Real.log (1 + δ * ∑ i, |g i x|) - Real.log (1 - ε) : ℝ) : EReal) ∂Q ≠
      ⊥ := by
    rw [hI]
    exact EReal.coe_ne_bot _
  have hI_top : ∫ᵉ x, ((Real.log (1 + δ * ∑ i, |g i x|) - Real.log (1 - ε) : ℝ) : EReal) ∂Q ≠
      ⊤ := by
    rw [hI]
    exact EReal.coe_ne_top _
  rw [eintegral_congr_ae (log_inv_rnDeriv_withDensity_inv_mul_ofReal_div hEm hg hδ.le hε1),
    eintegral_add (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop) (eintegrable_of_eintegral_ne_bot hI_bot)
      (.inr hI_top) (.inr hI_bot), hI, ← hsE, integral_sub hlogh0 (integrable_const _)]
  simp

/-- **The smallest relative entropy is at most the largest expected logarithm, on a set without
arbitrage**: when `Q` is carried by a set `Y` without
arbitrage that carries the null, and `log (1 + ∑ i, |g i|)` is `Q`-integrable, the smallest
relative entropy from `Q` to the null is at most the largest expected logarithm of an
e-variable. -/
theorem klInf_constraintNull_le_maxEPower_of_noArbitrageOn (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i))
    (hY : NoArbitrageOn g Y) (hYμ : ∀ ν ∈ constraintNull (range g), ν Yᶜ = 0)
    [IsProbabilityMeasure Q] (hQY : Q Yᶜ = 0)
    (hQ : Integrable (fun x ↦ Real.log (1 + ∑ i, |g i x|)) Q) :
    klInf Q (constraintNull (range g)) ≤ maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) := by
  have hS : ∀ μ ∈ constraintNull (range g), μ univ ≤ 1 :=
    fun _ hμ ↦ (isProbabilityMeasure_of_mem_constraintNull hμ).measure_univ.le
  set s := maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) with hs_def
  rcases eq_or_ne s ⊤ with hs | hs
  · rw [hs]
    exact le_top
  have hsE : s = ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (numeraire Q (constraintNull (range g)) x) ∂Q :=
    maxEPower_eq_eintegral_numeraire hS
  have hs0 : (0 : EReal) ≤ s := hsE ▸ (isNumeraire_numeraire Q hS).eintegral_log_nonneg hS
  have hs_bot : s ≠ ⊥ := ne_bot_of_le_ne_bot (by simp) hs0
  have hδ1 : ∀ n : ℕ, 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1) ≤ 1 := fun n ↦ div_le_one_of_le₀ (by simp) (by positivity)
  -- the damping tends to zero, by dominated convergence
  have hlim := hQ.tendsto_integral_log_one_add_mul (by fun_prop) (fun x ↦ by positivity)
    tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat (.of_forall fun n ↦ by positivity)
  -- choose the damping and the slack for a given margin
  rw [← EReal.le_of_forall_lt_iff_le]
  intro z hz
  have hs_eq : s = ((s.toReal : ℝ) : EReal) := (EReal.coe_toReal hs hs_bot).symm
  rw [hs_eq, EReal.coe_lt_coe_iff] at hz
  set η := z - s.toReal with hη_def
  have hη : 0 < η := by linarith
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (hlim.eventually (gt_mem_nhds (half_pos hη))).exists
  set ε := 1 - Real.exp (-(η / 2)) with hε_def
  have hε : 0 < ε := by
    have : Real.exp (-(η / 2)) < 1 := Real.exp_lt_one_iff.2 (by linarith)
    linarith
  have hε1 : ε < 1 := by
    have := Real.exp_pos (-(η / 2))
    linarith
  have hlogε : Real.log (1 - ε) = -(η / 2) := by
    rw [hε_def, sub_sub_cancel, Real.log_exp]
  refine (klInf_constraintNull_le_maxEPower_add hg hY hYμ hQY hQ hs
    (δ := 1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) (by positivity) (hδ1 n) hε hε1).trans ?_
  rw [← hs_def, hs_eq, ← EReal.coe_add, EReal.coe_le_coe_iff, hlogε]
  linarith

/-! ### E-variables and bets -/

/-- On a set `Y` without arbitrage that carries the null and `Q`, the largest expected logarithm
of an e-variable is at most that of a bet: every e-variable is at most a bet on `Y`, by the
complete class theorem [LRR26, Theorem 3.1]. -/
theorem maxEPower_constraintNull_le_iSup_eintegral_log_of_noArbitrageOn
    (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) (hY : NoArbitrageOn g Y)
    (hYμ : ∀ ν ∈ constraintNull (range g), ν Yᶜ = 0) (hQY : Q Yᶜ = 0) :
    maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) ≤
      ⨆ π ∈ constraintBets g,
        ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, (π i : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q := by
  refine maxEPower_le_iff.2 fun X hX ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨π, hπ, hXπ⟩ := hX.exists_mem_constraintBets_le_of_noArbitrageOn hg hY hYμ
  refine le_trans ?_ (le_iSup₂ (f := fun π (_ : π ∈ constraintBets g) ↦
    ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, (π i : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q) _ hπ)
  refine eintegral_mono_ae (Filter.eventually_of_mem (mem_ae_iff.2 hQY) fun x hx ↦ ?_)
  exact ENNReal.log_le_log (hXπ x hx)

/-- If a nonnegative combination of the constraints is nonnegative almost surely under every
member of the null and under a finite measure `Q`, and positive on a set of positive `Q`-measure,
then the bets have arbitrarily large expected logarithms under `Q`. -/
theorem iSup_eintegral_log_ofReal_one_add_eq_top (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i))
    [IsFiniteMeasure Q] {ρ : ι → ℝ} (hρ : ∀ i, 0 ≤ ρ i)
    (hρμ : ∀ μ ∈ constraintNull (range g), ∀ᵐ x ∂μ, 0 ≤ ∑ i, ρ i * g i x)
    (hρQ : ∀ᵐ x ∂Q, 0 ≤ ∑ i, ρ i * g i x) (hQρ : Q {x | 0 < ∑ i, ρ i * g i x} ≠ 0) :
    ⨆ π ∈ constraintBets g,
      ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, (π i : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hQc⟩ := exists_gt_measure_setOf_le_ne_zero hQρ
  set A := {x | c ≤ ∑ i, ρ i * g i x} with hA_def
  have hA : MeasurableSet A := measurableSet_le measurable_const (by fun_prop)
  set q := (Q A).toReal with hq_def
  have hq : 0 < q := ENNReal.toReal_pos hQc (measure_ne_top Q A)
  rw [EReal.eq_top_iff_forall_lt]
  intro y
  -- the bet with weights `t ρ` is at least `1`, and at least `1 + t c` on `A`
  set t := (Real.exp (|y| / q + 1) - 1) / c with ht_def
  have ht : 0 ≤ t := div_nonneg (by linarith [Real.one_le_exp (by positivity : 0 ≤ |y| / q + 1)])
    hc.le
  have hsum : ∀ x, ∑ i, ((t * ρ i).toNNReal : ℝ) * g i x = t * ∑ i, ρ i * g i x := fun x ↦ by
    simp only [Real.coe_toNNReal _ (mul_nonneg ht (hρ _)), mul_assoc, ← Finset.mul_sum]
  have hbet : (fun i ↦ (t * ρ i).toNNReal) ∈ constraintBets g := by
    refine mem_constraintBets_iff.2 fun μ hμ ↦ ?_
    filter_upwards [hρμ μ hμ] with x hx
    rw [hsum]
    have := mul_nonneg ht hx
    linarith
  have hlog : Real.log (1 + t * c) = |y| / q + 1 := by
    rw [ht_def, div_mul_cancel₀ _ hc.ne', add_sub_cancel, Real.log_exp]
  have hlow : ((Real.log (1 + t * c) * q : ℝ) : EReal) ≤
      ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, ((t * ρ i).toNNReal : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q := by
    have hlc : 0 ≤ Real.log (1 + t * c) := Real.log_nonneg (by nlinarith)
    calc ((Real.log (1 + t * c) * q : ℝ) : EReal)
        = ∫ᵉ x, ((A.indicator (fun _ ↦ ENNReal.ofReal (Real.log (1 + t * c))) x : ℝ≥0∞) :
            EReal) ∂Q := by
          have : ENNReal.ofReal (Real.log (1 + t * c)) * Q A =
              ENNReal.ofReal (Real.log (1 + t * c) * q) := by
            rw [ENNReal.ofReal_mul hlc, hq_def, ENNReal.ofReal_toReal (measure_ne_top Q A)]
          rw [eintegral_coe_ennreal, lintegral_indicator_const hA, this,
            EReal.coe_ennreal_ofReal, max_eq_left (mul_nonneg hlc hq.le)]
      _ ≤ _ := by
          refine eintegral_mono_ae ?_
          filter_upwards [hρQ] with x hx
          rw [hsum]
          have h1 : 0 < 1 + t * ∑ i, ρ i * g i x := by nlinarith
          rw [ENNReal.log_ofReal_of_pos h1]
          by_cases hxA : x ∈ A
          · have hcx : c ≤ ∑ i, ρ i * g i x := by simpa [hA_def] using hxA
            rw [indicator_of_mem hxA, EReal.coe_ennreal_ofReal, max_eq_left hlc,
              EReal.coe_le_coe_iff]
            exact Real.log_le_log (by nlinarith) (by nlinarith [hcx])
          · rw [indicator_of_notMem hxA, EReal.coe_ennreal_zero, ← EReal.coe_zero,
              EReal.coe_le_coe_iff]
            exact Real.log_nonneg (by nlinarith)
  calc (y : EReal) < ((Real.log (1 + t * c) * q : ℝ) : EReal) := by
        rw [hlog, EReal.coe_lt_coe_iff]
        nlinarith [le_abs_self y, abs_nonneg y, div_mul_cancel₀ |y| hq.ne']
    _ ≤ _ := hlow
    _ ≤ _ := le_iSup₂ (f := fun π (_ : π ∈ constraintBets g) ↦
        ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, (π i : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q) _ hbet

/-- **The largest e-power is the supremum of the expected logarithms of the bets**: for
finitely many measurable constraints `g i` and a finite measure `Q`, the largest expected
logarithm under `Q` of an e-variable for the null is the supremum of the expected logarithms of
the bets `1 + ∑ i, π i * g i`. The expected logarithm of a bet is `⊥` when the bet vanishes or is
negative on a set of positive `Q`-measure. This follows [EVR26, Note 20]. -/
theorem maxEPower_constraintNull_eq_iSup_eintegral_log (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i))
    (Q : Measure 𝓧) [IsFiniteMeasure Q] :
    maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) =
      ⨆ π ∈ constraintBets g,
        ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, (π i : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (iSup₂_le fun π hπ ↦
    (isEVar_ofReal_one_add_of_mem_constraintBets hg hπ).eintegral_log_le_maxEPower Q)
  obtain ⟨Y, -, hYμ, hQY, hY⟩ | ⟨ρ, hρ, hρμ, hρQ, hQρ⟩ :=
    exists_measurableSet_noArbitrageOn_or_exists_sum_mul_pos hg Q
  · exact maxEPower_constraintNull_le_iSup_eintegral_log_of_noArbitrageOn hg hY hYμ hQY
  · rw [iSup_eintegral_log_ofReal_one_add_eq_top hg hρ hρμ hρQ hQρ]
    exact le_top

/-! ### The dual formula -/

/-- **The smallest relative entropy to the null is its largest e-power**, the largest expected
logarithm of an e-variable: for finitely many measurable constraints `g i` and a probability
measure `Q` under which every `log⁺ |g i|` is integrable, with no constraint qualification. The
null may be empty: both sides are then `⊤`. This follows [EVR26, Note 20]. -/
theorem klInf_constraintNull_eq_maxEPower {κ : Type*} [Finite κ] {g : κ → 𝓧 → ℝ}
    (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i)) (Q : Measure 𝓧) [IsProbabilityMeasure Q]
    (hQ : ∀ i, Integrable (fun x ↦ Real.posLog (g i x)) Q) :
    klInf Q (constraintNull (range g)) = maxEPower Q (constraintNull (range g)) := by
  have := Fintype.ofFinite κ
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (maxEPower_le_klInf fun _ hP ↦
    (isProbabilityMeasure_of_mem_constraintNull hP).measure_univ.le)
  obtain ⟨Y, -, hYμ, hQY, hY⟩ | ⟨ρ, hρ, hρμ, hρQ, hQρ⟩ :=
    exists_measurableSet_noArbitrageOn_or_exists_sum_mul_pos hg Q
  · exact klInf_constraintNull_le_maxEPower_of_noArbitrageOn hg hY hYμ hQY
      (integrable_log_one_add_sum_abs (fun i ↦ (hg i).aemeasurable) hQ)
  · rw [maxEPower_constraintNull_eq_iSup_eintegral_log hg Q,
      iSup_eintegral_log_ofReal_one_add_eq_top hg hρ hρμ hρQ hQρ]
    exact le_top

/-- **The dual formula for the smallest relative entropy to a null generated by finitely many
constraints**: for measurable constraints `g i` and a probability measure `Q` under which every
`log⁺ |g i|` is integrable, the smallest relative entropy from `Q` to the null is the supremum of
the expected logarithms of the bets `1 + ∑ i, π i * g i`, with no constraint qualification. The
formulas of [HT15] for one mean constraint are cases of it. This follows [EVR26, Note 20]. -/
theorem klInf_constraintNull_eq_iSup_eintegral_log (hg : ∀ i, Measurable (g i))
    (Q : Measure 𝓧) [IsProbabilityMeasure Q]
    (hQ : ∀ i, Integrable (fun x ↦ Real.posLog (g i x)) Q) :
    klInf Q (constraintNull (range g)) =
      ⨆ π ∈ constraintBets g,
        ∫ᵉ x, ENNReal.log (ENNReal.ofReal (1 + ∑ i, (π i : ℝ) * g i x)) ∂Q := by
  rw [klInf_constraintNull_eq_maxEPower hg Q hQ,
    maxEPower_constraintNull_eq_iSup_eintegral_log hg Q]

end ProbabilityTheory
